  <data name="ErrorAuth" xml:space="preserve"><value>YouTube treats this connection as a bot. The app needs a normal browser session — not a Google password here, but cookies from a site you already opened.&#x0a;&#x0a;1. Open this same video in Firefox or Edge as a normal website and refresh.&#x0a;2. Come back here and try again (paste the link / download).&#x0a;3. You can leave the browser open. YtPump reads only YouTube cookies and does not receive logins, passwords, or browsing history.&#x0a;&#x0a;Use Firefox or Edge. Current Chrome encrypts cookies so third-party programs usually cannot read them. Opening the video in Chrome usually does not help — even if you are signed in to a Google account.&#x0a;&#x0a;This is not a network outage or a proxy problem.</value></data>
  <data name="ErrorCookiesMissing" xml:space="preserve"><value>Firefox or Edge was not found.&#x0a;&#x0a;YouTube treats this connection as a bot. A normal browser session is required.&#x0a;&#x0a;1. Install Firefox or Edge and open this video there as a website.&#x0a;2. Refresh the page and come back here.&#x0a;&#x0a;Current Chrome encrypts cookies so YtPump usually cannot read them. Opening the video in Chrome will not help, even if you are signed in to a Google account. This is not a network outage or a proxy problem.</value></data>
